{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let Reuben live and not die.</b> When he passes before the vanguard before his brothers, as the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben stipulated — not one of them shall die in war." "<b>And let his men be a number.</b> In that same number in which they pass they shall return, so that none of them remains. Or, אל ימות above is its referent, meaning: let not his dead be a number, that they increase, and let them not be counted as many."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:59.901237105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}